    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d158">

                <pb facs="0359" n="285" sameAs="frus:frus1941-43/pg285"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Roosevelt Papers: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Prime Minister Churchill to President Roosevelt
                    </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d158-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">immediate</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">most secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Ottawa</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-12-30">December 30 [1941.]</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Following for President from Prime Minister.</p>
                <p>Naturally both the declaration and the Unity Plan, having to be referred to so
                    many different parts will require final review by us on Thursday afternoon.
                    Meanwhile as I am out of touch I hope you will discuss outstanding minor points
                    on declaration with Halifax, and points raised by H. M. Government on Unity Plan
                    with Pound after they have been considered by our (Mission?). In principle,
                    everything seems settled, but I expect it will take till the end of week <pb
                        facs="0360" n="286" xml:id="pg286"/> to get final fair copies. This will be
                    a pretty considerable achievement.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
